+## ECON-02B2d4c3 — Node-free native factory construction host (2026-10-31)
+
+The C++17 `galaxy_factory_local_host` executable now serves the existing Factory Designer and its trusted colony construction API **from one native process**. Players no longer need to launch the Node.js development server to make real, journaled factory construction steps. It opens only an existing SQLite world, binds a session-restricted **127.0.0.1** listener, and packs the viewer assets alongside its binary. The default browser opens automatically; Windows can use an OS save picker when no `--db` is supplied. Linux developer example: `./build/galaxy_factory_local_host --db /path/to/EXISTING.sqlite`. The original `galaxy_factory_host_bridge` and Node test server remain for compatibility.
+
+The new Linux code passes **60/60 non-live and 26/26 live/relay CTests**, **93/93 JavaScript tests**, **3/3 design tests**, and native HTTP/restart/cancellation checks; these are two disjoint native runs, not a single uninterrupted one. Offline Chromium UI passed, but direct native-browser localhost navigation is blocked by the container policy, and Windows compilation/interactive acceptance is not yet complete. **This is not yet integrated into the main space-game GUI, and walls/doors/floors and NPC construction crews remain future work.** See [the engineering report](docs/engineering/ECON02B2d4c3_Native_Factory_Runtime_2026-10-31.md).
